# Inventory Management System Implementation Walkthrough

The Inventory Management System has been successfully integrated into the Cloud Kitchen project across 6 seamless, non-disruptive phases without altering or disrupting any existing customer ordering or admin features.

---

## 📸 Key Features & Architecture Highlights

### 1. Database Relational Architecture (Phase 1)
- **`Ingredients` Table**: Stores central raw stock (e.g. Paneer, Cheese, Milk, Flour, Oil, Spices, Vegetables) with unit metrics, cost per unit, and low stock thresholds.
- **`Dish_Ingredients` Table**: Recipe relation mapping 1 dish (`m_id`) to multiple central raw ingredients (`ingredient_id`) with specific quantity ratios (`qty_required`).
- **`menu_item` Extensions**: Added `m_track_inventory` (BIT, default 1) and `m_unit_stock` (INT, default NULL).

```mermaid
erDiagram
    menu_item ||--o{ Dish_Ingredients : "has recipe mapping"
    Ingredients ||--o{ Dish_Ingredients : "used in dishes"
    menu_item {
        int m_id PK
        string m_name
        decimal m_final_price
        string m_availability
        bit m_track_inventory
        int m_unit_stock
    }
    Ingredients {
        int ingredient_id PK
        string ingredient_name
        decimal stock_quantity
        string unit
        decimal cost_per_unit
        decimal low_stock_threshold
        datetime last_updated
    }
    Dish_Ingredients {
        int recipe_id PK
        int m_id FK
        int ingredient_id FK
        decimal qty_required
    }
```

